  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "In a radioactive decay chain reaction, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mrow/><mn>90</mn><mn>230</mn></msubsup><mi>Th</mi></math>&nbsp;nucleus decays into <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Po</mi><mprescripts/><mn>84</mn><mn>214</mn></mmultiscripts></math>&nbsp;nucleus. The ratio of the number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math> to number of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;particles emitted in this process is _______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi></math>&nbsp;particles are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#946;</mi></math>&nbsp;particles are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub></math>.</p><p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mrow/><mn>90</mn></msub><msup><mi>Th</mi><mn>230</mn></msup><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#8594;</mo><mn>84</mn></msub><msup><mi>Po</mi><mn>214</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub><mi>&#946;</mi></math>.</p><p>Change in mass number is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>230</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>214</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p>Number of proton,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>90</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>a</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>So, the ratio,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#945;</mi></msub><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>&#946;</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
